{
  "id": "liyuan_opera",
  "name": "Liyuanxi (Quanzhou Pear Garden opera)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Minnan-language opera of Quanzhou, one of the oldest surviving descendants of Song and Yuan southern drama, with a refined, slow and highly codified movement style; it is on China's national intangible heritage list (2006). It is sung to nanyin music: the nanyin instruments, pipa, sanxian, dongxiao and erxian, with paiban clappers accompany the singers, while the drummer leads on the nangu, pressing a foot on the drumhead to bend its pitch, and the small aizai shawm marks set pieces. The xiao, erhu and suona cards stand for the dongxiao, erxian and aizai.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-2000s liyuanxi, art Music, east Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. pipa, sanxian, purple bamboo phyllostachys canonical literati premium xiao, python skin snake skin bamboo stick horsehair threaded between strings erhu, paiban, acoustic membrane drum, shrill high rosewood bodied copper belled suona. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
